vkd3d: Write a null descriptor for a buffer view of no elements.

A buffer SRV or UAV with NumElements 0 went to vkCreateBufferView with a range
of 0, which Vulkan does not allow (VUID-VkBufferViewCreateInfo-range-00928).
Most drivers make an empty view of it. KosmicKrisp asks Metal for a texture of
width 0, and Metal's descriptor validation aborts the process:

  -[MTLTextureDescriptorInternal validateWithDevice:]: failed assertion
  `MTLTextureDescriptor has width of zero.'
    mtl_new_texture_with_descriptor_linear
    kk_CreateBufferView
    vkCreateBufferView

The Last of Us Part II Remastered makes such a view on its main thread a few
seconds after its swap chain, and never got a frame out.

A null descriptor reads as zero, which is what Direct3D 12 gives for a read
out of the bounds of a view; both callers already write one when there is no
view.

Applied by macos/build-vkd3d-proton.sh to github.com/athei/vkd3d-proton at
c5e2c9b8c55872893e3ba47d60448dd4f35185ef. Written with an AI assistant
(Claude); vkd3d-proton states no policy on that.
---
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
index 794e8b25..64573bcb 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
@@ -6423,6 +6423,16 @@ static bool vkd3d_buffer_view_get_aligned_view(
         }
     }
 
+    if (!num_elements)
+    {
+        /* Vulkan has no buffer view of no elements: the range of one must be greater than 0,
+         * and KosmicKrisp asks Metal for a texture of width 0 for it, which aborts the process.
+         * A null descriptor reads as zero, which is what a read out of the bounds of a view
+         * gives in Direct3D 12, and every read of this view is one. */
+        *view = NULL;
+        return true;
+    }
+
     if (!vkd3d_create_buffer_view_for_resource(device, resource, format,
             first_element, num_elements,
             structured_stride, vk_flags, view))
